WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.970
- Today I'm having strangers meet

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.690
and have a conversation
without seeing each other.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.470
Make sure you stick around to the end

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.829
to watch them meet face to
face for the first time.

00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:15.060
(calm music)

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.100
- Wanna ask a question?

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.102
- Okay. Yep.
- Go for it.

00:00:17.102 --> 00:00:17.935
- I'll go first.

00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:19.770
(both chuckle)

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.360
- Ready?
- Yeah.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.490
- What's something I
wouldn't believe about you?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.789
- What made you stop loving someone?

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:26.760
(laughing)

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.410
- Can I choose a different one?

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.278
- [Speaker] If you want, yeah.

00:00:29.278 --> 00:00:30.148
- That's up to you.

00:00:30.148 --> 00:00:31.068
- Hold on, let me see.

00:00:31.068 --> 00:00:33.754
(both laughing)

00:00:33.754 --> 00:00:35.377
Let me choose a different one.

00:00:35.377 --> 00:00:36.990
(all laughing)

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.250
- Oh God.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.540
Finish the sentence,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.790
I wish I had told my ex.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.743
- I wish I had told my ex.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.681
- Blank, yeah.

00:00:45.681 --> 00:00:48.348
(both laughing)

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.589
- Oh my God.

00:00:54.589 --> 00:00:55.800
(laughing)

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.503
- Why you gotta go so deep with me, bro?

00:00:57.503 --> 00:00:59.820
- I just, I do what the cards tell me.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.223
- Okay. Okay.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.590
- I wish I had told them
that my internal pain

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:08.540
wasn't their fault.

00:01:09.598 --> 00:01:10.650
- Mm.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:11.640
Wow. Okay.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.637
- What about you?

00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:14.850
(both laughing)

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.380
- I wish I had told my ex

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.839
that I wish we slowed things down more

00:01:18.839 --> 00:01:22.260
instead of moving so
fast in our relationship.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.130
- Yeah.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.980
- Because I feel like as fast as we moved

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.548
it helped bring our
relationship to an end.

00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:30.860
- Ooh.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.569
I wish I had told my ex that I
understand his addiction now.

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:37.200
I just never understood it all that well.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.530
And he'd had addiction issues
since he was nine years old.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.140
So there's just so much
more like development

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.978
that he had had based
around substances and yeah,

00:01:46.978 --> 00:01:50.343
I just, I would tell them that.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.030
- What's something I
wouldn't believe about you?

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.243
- What's something you
wouldn't believe about me?

00:01:56.243 --> 00:01:58.500
There's something that most people

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.210
wouldn't believe about me,

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.970
but that's because they can see me.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:03.803
- Okay.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.279
- I've lost 175 pounds.

00:02:07.279 --> 00:02:08.112
(gasps)

00:02:08.112 --> 00:02:08.945
- Oh my goodness.

00:02:08.945 --> 00:02:10.350
- So maybe you won't believe that about me

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.970
once you see me at the end of this.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.230
But other than that, I don't know.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.340
- That's incredible.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.213
- I am a gigantic sports fan.

00:02:18.213 --> 00:02:19.046
- Really.

00:02:19.046 --> 00:02:19.879
(laughing)

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:21.660
- People meet me and the first...

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.130
That's not the first
thing they think about me.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.410
So when football season rolls around

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.990
and I'm like ready to go,

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.136
I'm not really great at
either of those sports,

00:02:30.136 --> 00:02:31.440
but I love them.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.391
- You love watching them.

00:02:32.391 --> 00:02:33.360
(laughing)

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.947
- What's something I
wouldn't believe about you?

00:02:35.947 --> 00:02:38.882
(calm music)

00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:41.063
- I almost died multiple times.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:42.900
- In Chicago?

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.250
- Yeah.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.080
I never thought I would see 25.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.690
'Cause a lot of my homies and
a lot of my family members

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.160
died before 25.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:50.993
- Right.

00:02:50.993 --> 00:02:52.350
- What about yourself?

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.300
- I always told myself 23.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.140
- Right.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.433
- When I hit 23,

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.746
this is like when I was
like 14 and like growing up,

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:03.120
I was like, "Once I hit
23, I'll be old enough.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.620
I've seen enough of the world."

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.453
- Right.

00:03:05.453 --> 00:03:06.360
- "I'm just gonna go out."

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.830
- Right. Just-

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.540
- Better by my own hands than
someone else's, you know?

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.370
And then I hit 23 and I'm like,
"Wait, life's pretty good.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.120
There's some good stuff out here."

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:15.953
And then I'm like, "Well,

00:03:15.953 --> 00:03:18.630
maybe when I'm older and
I'm 25" and I'm like, "Man,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:19.740
why didn't I ever think that way?"

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:20.820
- Right.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.080
Said, I ain't going no more.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.800
I'm gonna see 35, for sure.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:24.932
- Yeah. And then 45.

00:03:24.932 --> 00:03:26.340
You've got a long life ahead of you.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.210
- Yeah.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.514
- How old are you?

00:03:28.514 --> 00:03:29.347
- I'm 26.

00:03:29.347 --> 00:03:30.689
- 25.

00:03:30.689 --> 00:03:31.522
- Oh, 25.

00:03:31.522 --> 00:03:32.355
- Oh, 25. Okay.
- Yeah.

00:03:32.355 --> 00:03:35.280
So we going through a lot life that's...

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.360
You know, we still learning.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.520
- Yeah. It feels like an age

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:39.353
where you're supposed to know everything,

00:03:39.353 --> 00:03:40.450
but you don't know anything.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:44.430
- I have a lot of older
people that tell me like,

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.810
you know, you're not
really gonna know anything

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.550
till at least 30.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.870
Like your life really doesn't start

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:49.724
till you're 30 years old. You know?

00:03:49.724 --> 00:03:51.360
- Yeah.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.980
- And from then on and then forth,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.380
you're gonna know all the
mistakes you made in the past

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:58.080
that you don't want to continue to make.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.610
- Yeah, I'm still making them though.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:01.691
- Yeah. Hey, we still
young though, brother.

00:04:01.691 --> 00:04:02.942
- Yeah, thank you.
- We still young.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.650
- All my friends are always like, "Man,

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:05.483
you're so old."

00:04:05.483 --> 00:04:08.183
I'm in my twenties, what
are you talking about?

00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:10.200
- I'm 26. They telling me I'm 30 already.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.033
- Yeah, exactly.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.480
God, don't do that to me.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.180
- Like, not yet.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:18.390
I try to pick up my views
in life a little bit faster

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:22.116
because I always had to live
older when I was younger.

00:04:22.116 --> 00:04:23.100
- I feel that.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.210
- Yeah.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.500
- You can't let go of
your youth though, man.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.333
- Yeah.

00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:30.210
- You gotta maintain some
childlike wonder about the world.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.530
- Yeah.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.350
- What's a song lyric that
reminds you of someone.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.060
- I don't know if you've ever
heard the song "Fine Line"

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.380
by Harry Styles?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.210
- I don't think I've heard
that one specifically.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.047
- Well, there's a song lyric that says,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:44.280
"Put a price on emotion. I'm
looking for something to buy."

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.930
And that lyric,

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.340
I would say it reminds
me of like my past self

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.470
just because for a while, like,

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:57.120
I just kind of felt like I
didn't feel anything like at all.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:57.953
- Yeah.

00:04:57.953 --> 00:04:59.130
- And so I'd be constantly looking

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.760
for like short term
things to make me happy.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.830
- Yeah. Like get that quick dopamine cake.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.663
- Yeah. Exactly.

00:05:05.663 --> 00:05:06.496
- Yeah.

00:05:06.496 --> 00:05:08.550
- And so I think like putting
a price on like emotion,

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.699
like on anything and like I'm
looking for something to buy.

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:13.710
I don't know, whenever
I first heard that song

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:14.550
I was going through that time

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:16.560
and it actually really
got me through a lot.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.820
How about you?

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.430
- Oh God. There's one called Icarus.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.100
The story of Icarus in Greek mythology

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.410
is where he's got like wax wings

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.410
and he flies too close the
sun and he plummets down.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.907
And it kind of reminds
me of my dad, honestly,

00:05:32.907 --> 00:05:37.907
because he just, he put himself
out there for everybody.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.443
- Yeah.

00:05:39.443 --> 00:05:41.240
- And he did so much and he tried so hard,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.670
but he never reached out.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:45.503
- Yeah.

00:05:45.503 --> 00:05:48.900
- And I feel like he just
ran so low on stamina

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.240
that just like in the heat
of the moment, you know,

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.910
he ended up taking his own life

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.940
but he just burned so bright for so long.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:57.993
- Wow.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.750
Wow.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.790
I'm so sorry about your dad.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.960
- It's good. Thank you though.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:04.793
- Thank you.

00:06:06.253 --> 00:06:08.250
- I don't know about
a specific lyric, but-

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.360
- You can say a song.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.930
- A whole song would be "Just
Like Heaven" by The Cure.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:13.763
- Yeah.

00:06:13.763 --> 00:06:16.212
- Because I just heard it a lot growing up

00:06:16.212 --> 00:06:20.550
and my mom told me she wants
it played at her funeral.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:21.570
- Right.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.340
- But like, it sucks.
That's such a good song.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.470
So now every time I hear it I get sad,

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.760
but I wanna still enjoy it.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.590
- Yeah. I relate to that.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:29.423
- What about you?

00:06:29.423 --> 00:06:31.533
- The song is called
"Bang Bros" by Lil Durk.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:33.960
Every time I hear that song

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.730
it reminds me of my brother that passed

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.760
because it's something
we used to listen to

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.350
before he died.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:41.340
- Right.

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.230
- And it just, every time
I hear it, it just...

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.077
That's why I like to space that
song out when I listen to it

00:06:46.077 --> 00:06:47.430
and I hear it too much.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:48.263
- Definitely.

00:06:48.263 --> 00:06:49.096
- Just 'cause every time I hear it,

00:06:49.096 --> 00:06:51.273
I want it to just be a
strong memory for me.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.367
- If you don't mind me
asking, how'd he pass?

00:06:55.367 --> 00:07:00.367
- He was murdered at a house
party in October, 2013.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:03.630
- Yeah.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:04.463
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:07:04.463 --> 00:07:05.296
- Yeah.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.750
- So what part of Chicago were
you in if that was happening?

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:10.650
- South side?

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:11.910
- Yeah.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.400
- It's a strong part of our life. Like-

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.233
- Definitely.

00:07:15.233 --> 00:07:16.560
- As much as we try to get away from it,

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.327
it's hard to get away from it

00:07:18.327 --> 00:07:20.970
because it's just a everyday thing for me.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.370
Like, you know, everybody
don't grow up the same.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.830
But where I came from,
where I grew up, it's just,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:26.940
it was just a part of my life

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:28.800
that I try the best to get away from.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.140
It's one strong reason
why I came to California

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.613
because like I knew that if I stayed there

00:07:33.613 --> 00:07:35.850
more worse things was
gonna keep happening.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:36.683
So I'm like,

00:07:36.683 --> 00:07:38.370
if I could have a chance to
come out here and stay out here,

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.600
I'm gonna stay out here.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.100
And I feel like as a man,

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.110
it made me a better man out here

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:45.360
where I'm not a angry person.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.430
- Yeah. That's important.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:48.643
I know a lot of men like that.

00:07:48.643 --> 00:07:49.740
- Yeah.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.573
- They just wanna...

00:07:50.573 --> 00:07:51.406
They got something on their shoulder

00:07:51.406 --> 00:07:52.380
and they can't get rid of it.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:53.460
- Yeah.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:56.235
- What's the most heroic
thing you've ever done?

00:07:56.235 --> 00:07:58.015
- Oh goodness.

00:07:58.015 --> 00:07:58.932
I mean I...

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:00.893
Oh yeah.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:06.720
I saved my grandpa and my
grandpa's dog from the pool once,

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.580
I was like 13 years old.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.240
They had like a 14 year old
dog that was blind and deaf

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.920
and it walked straight into the pool.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.200
My grandpa jumps in and
then he starts drowning.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.940
The dog is like above water.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.159
My grandpa's under the water

00:08:19.159 --> 00:08:23.280
and then none of my family
responded, so I just jumped in.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.770
I guess that's heroic
in a way. I don't know.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.930
Saved both the dog and my grandpa.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:30.090
- Yeah. Saved a double drowning. That's...

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:30.923
Yeah, for sure.

00:08:30.923 --> 00:08:33.489
That's hero level quality, air fist bump.

00:08:33.489 --> 00:08:34.777
(laughing)
Bam.

00:08:34.777 --> 00:08:35.880
By the end of this,

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.043
I'm curious how many we actually lined up.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:40.824
- The fist bump? Probably
only one. That one.

00:08:40.824 --> 00:08:43.650
Yeah. 'Cause I was like, yeah.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.599
And then I didn't actually
do it, so I apologize.

00:08:45.599 --> 00:08:48.980
I apologize for not actually following-

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:49.856
- I'm so hurt.

00:08:49.856 --> 00:08:50.993
- I know. I'm so sorry,

00:08:50.993 --> 00:08:53.400
(indistinct) so rough from
the outside perspective.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.566
- I'm just over here looking
like an absolute fool.

00:08:55.566 --> 00:08:56.399
- Okay.

00:08:56.399 --> 00:08:57.537
- My family's gonna watch this.

00:08:57.537 --> 00:08:58.370
- All right, okay.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.900
Well, what if we do this?
We hold one up right now.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.460
Right now. And then smile for the camera.

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:03.293
- Okay. Yeah.

00:09:03.293 --> 00:09:04.126
Are you ready?

00:09:04.126 --> 00:09:04.959
- Yes.

00:09:04.959 --> 00:09:05.792
- Okay, cool, I got it.

00:09:05.792 --> 00:09:06.840
(laughing)

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.430
- Are we still doing it?

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:09.379
- Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. Totally.

00:09:09.379 --> 00:09:11.220
(both laughing)

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:12.401
- All right. I know
you're messing with now.

00:09:12.401 --> 00:09:14.400
(both laughing)

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.687
Yeah, okay. What about you?

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.708
- I used to work in a
psychiatric hospital for kids.

00:09:20.708 --> 00:09:21.640
- Oooh.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:26.490
- So I saved a couple kids
from like ending things.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.230
- Oh my gosh. Yeah, that's incredible.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.063
- Yeah.

00:09:29.063 --> 00:09:30.270
- Congratulations.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.187
- Thank you. Yeah.

00:09:31.187 --> 00:09:32.580
